**Ended on: ipa1 + THP re-home (gen_layout/gen_powp r11 adoption) after building and refuting the gen_pow2-style one-sweep GT-split family with counters — best tryout (a80n0 leased core via tryout.sh): L=100 B=1 4393.0 us/xform (2.30x MKL best-window 1.91x same-window), batched 40 B=8 159.7 / 50 B=4 410.9 us/xform; rel L2 = 3.6–4.5e-16 (chains 3.8–5.0e-14 vs tol 1e-10, all exact historical values).**

What the round did:

- **Shipped: THP re-home** at vbytes ≥ 8 MiB (state + staged-c in a `gl_map_huge` arena, zero extra copies, race arena = plan arena for trial fidelity, wisdom tag chain7→chain8). Node: dtlb walks 6910→99/step (−98.6%), 8/11 held-lease pairs, quiet floors 4416.7 vs 4490.5. Final quiet window: **4393.0, sd 0.08%** — this cell's best-ever print for this entry (r11 board was 4554.7).
- **Built, measured, refuted: the one-sweep family ipw1** (x-stage DFT4/DFT25 split across the chain-step seam, in-place class-major custody, exactly the transfer gen_pow2's r11 note proposed for 100=4×25). It loses +16–25% on Ice Lake (5 pairs + 3 interleaved races) and +18% on SPR. The differential PMU nails why: under ipa1 the step's **demand LLC misses are only ~0.4 MB against the 80 MB/step stream** — the DRAM is fully prefetch-covered under the passes, so there was nothing to delete, while the sweep adds a volume-level tail pass + a 4 MB L3 staging round trip (l1d.replacement +23%). This refutes my own r11 "88% DRAM-BW-bound" claim with my own engine's counters and settles the r11 cross-entry disagreement on gen_pfa_small's side (latency/overlap-bound). Kept raced at rank last as xarch insurance; the noise gate cannot promote it.
- **Everything gate-clean**: bit-identical outputs across all forced picks and rehome/norehome, exact historical gate values at 40/50/75/80/100/112/117 plus the 100 B=2 off-case, 5/5 cold-create determinism with the new pool, hot kernels nm-size-identical to r11, no L=40/50 regression (159.7 / 410.9 = board floors). Strategy record appended with full attribution (gen_layout, gen_powp, gen_pow2, gen_pfa_small, gen_dense_prime); all my wisdom keys stripped under flock per protocol.
